# ─── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# https://platform.claude.com → API keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Supabase → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → Transaction pooler
# NOTE: if your password contains @ % # / : or ?, percent-encode it (@ → %40).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.xxxx:PASSWORD@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Where this app is reachable. Used in magic-link redirects.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Required only for the scheduled publishing worker (/api/cron/publish).
# Without it the route returns 503 rather than running unsecured.
CRON_SECRET=

# Set to 1 to serve every Claude call from test/mock-anthropic.ts fixtures.
# The whole pipeline then runs offline, with no API key and no spend.
MOCK_ANTHROPIC=0

# ─── Email (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gmail SMTP, the same transport week 3 uses. Without these, the newsletter is
# still approved, formatted and queued — it is released for a person to send
# by hand rather than delivered by the app, and the publication row records
# which of the two happened. GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD is an App Password from the
# Google account, not the account password.
GMAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
MAIL_FROM_NAME=Koya Talent

# ─── Live posting (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, X and LinkedIn posts are queued and released for a person to
# publish by hand — the app records which of the two happened.
#
# Encrypts OAuth tokens at rest. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# Changing it invalidates every stored connection.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# X app (developer.x.com) — OAuth 2.0, Confidential client, with write access.
# Callback URL to register: {APP_URL}/api/admin/channels/x/callback
# Scopes requested: tweet.read tweet.write users.read offline.access
X_CLIENT_ID=UVpaLU1GODI0a19CYU1oVGdmZDg6MTpjaQ
X_CLIENT_SECRET=WXQnvfJ0yXIdNDg5pnDlsETcZkYv79uKaxpVI6e133z482hjIO

# LinkedIn app (linkedin.com/developers) with the Community Management product.
# Callback URL to register: {APP_URL}/api/admin/channels/linkedin/callback
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Who the posts are authored by. A company page needs w_organization_social and
# an admin role on that page; leave unset to post as the connecting member.
#   LINKEDIN_AUTHOR_URN=urn:li:organization:12345
LINKEDIN_AUTHOR_URN=


For the X developer console, the callback / redirect URI is:

https://koya-content-agent.vercel.app/api/admin/channels/x/callback

That's the route I built at app/api/admin/channels/[channel]/callback/route.ts, and it's constructed in lib/oauth/providers.ts as ${APP_URL}/api/admin/channels/x/callback. It must match exactly — X rejects the authorization request if the redirect_uri differs from a registered one by even a trailing slash.

Two things worth knowing while you're in there:

Register your local one too. X lets you add multiple callback URIs, so add:
http://localhost:3000/api/admin/channels/x/callback
Whichever you use has to match APP_URL in the environment that's running, since the app builds the URI from that variable rather than from the incoming request.

Also on the app settings page:
- Type of App → Web App, Automated App or Bot (this is the Confidential Client option — the token exchange uses HTTP Basic auth with your client secret, which a public client wouldn't have)
- App permissions → Read and write (the default is read-only, and tweet.write won't be granted without this)
- Website URL → https://koya-content-agent.vercel.app

The scopes the app requests are tweet.read tweet.write users.read offline.access — those are set in code, not in the console. offline.access is the one that matters most: without it there's no refresh token, the access token dies after two hours, and every scheduled post after that fails.

For LinkedIn, the equivalent is the same shape with the channel swapped:
https://koya-content-agent.vercel.app/api/admin/channels/linkedin/callback